{"name":"Programs: fetch as a thin node","description":"Test demo: run a thin node, hear the haves of a super node, fetch a signed program on demand and run it","kind":"thin","entry":"thin.txt","args":["10.0.2.2:7020","03e489240a78d8a85713f5b6d22749632d8268e238c40b9aca99f54c44de11828d","Downloaded: fib and primes"]}This app holds no program. It runs a thin programnetwork node, which
stores nothing for others and announces nothing. It subscribes to the
node its args give, hears its haves, and fetches the program its args name
on demand. It checks the signer key of its args and every block hash, then
runs the program.
See "Node types (#34)" in docs/ProgramDistribution.md.
